IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 12 -- Application of particular State laws to coastal waters (ss 47 to 47G).
-- The Crimes at Sea Act 2001, section 3 and the two Commonwealth Coastal Waters Acts are not among the sources;
-- whether a thing is within them is an input.

§ `Part 12 -- Application of particular State laws to coastal waters`

§§ `s 47 -- Definitions for pt 12`

-- src:896 | cooperative scheme means the cooperative scheme as defined under the Crimes at Sea Act 2001, section 3.
@ref s 47, definition cooperative scheme (src:896-896)
GIVEN `it is the cooperative scheme as defined under the Crimes at Sea Act 2001, section 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the scheme is the cooperative scheme (s 47, definition cooperative scheme)` IS
    JUST `it is the cooperative scheme as defined under the Crimes at Sea Act 2001, section 3`

-- src:897 | criminal laws means the substantive criminal law, and the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, within the meaning of the cooperative scheme.
@ref s 47, definition criminal laws (src:897-897)
GIVEN `it is the substantive criminal law, or the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, within the meaning of the cooperative scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law is a criminal law (s 47, definition criminal laws)` IS
    JUST `it is the substantive criminal law, or the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, within the meaning of the cooperative scheme`

-- "laws of the State means the laws, whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural, that are from time to time in force in the State, but does not include (a) laws of the Commonwealth; or (b) criminal laws."
-- src:898 | laws of the State means the laws, whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural, that are from time to time in force in the State, but does not include—
-- src:899 | (a) laws of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:900 | (b) criminal laws.
@ref s 47, definition laws of the State (src:898-900)
GIVEN `it is a law, whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural, that is from time to time in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a criminal law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law is a law of the State (s 47, definition laws of the State)` IS
    JUST (`it is a law, whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural, that is from time to time in force in the State` AND (NOT `it is a law of the Commonwealth`) AND (NOT `it is a criminal law`))

§§ `ss 47A to 47E`

DECLARE `Place` IS ONE OF
    `the coastal waters of the State`
    `the seabed and subsoil beneath the coastal waters of the State`
    `the airspace above the coastal waters of the State`
    `any other place`

-- src:902 | The laws of the State apply in and in relation to—
-- src:903 | (a) the coastal waters of the State; and
-- src:904 | (b) the seabed and subsoil beneath, and the airspace above, the coastal waters of the State;
-- src:905 | as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State.
@ref s 47A (src:902-905)
GIVEN `the law is a law of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the laws of the State apply in and in relation to the place (s 47A)` IS
    IF NOT `the law is a law of the State`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER place
        WHEN `any other place` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1): "Nothing in this part makes a provision applicable in or in relation to a particular place" in cases (a), (b), (c).
-- src:907 | (1) Nothing in this part makes a provision of the laws of the State applicable in or in relation to a particular place—
-- src:908 | (a) to the extent the provision is incapable of applying in or in relation to that place; or
-- src:909 | (b) if those laws expressly provide that the provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place; or
-- src:910 | (c) if those laws expressly provide that the provision applies only in a stated locality in the State that does not include that place.
@ref s 47B(1) (src:907-910)
GIVEN `the provision is incapable of applying in or in relation to that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those laws expressly provide that the provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those laws expressly provide that the provision applies only in a stated locality in the State that does not include that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this part makes the provision applicable in or in relation to the place (s 47B(1))` IS
    IF    `the provision is incapable of applying in or in relation to that place`
       OR `those laws expressly provide that the provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place`
       OR `those laws expressly provide that the provision applies only in a stated locality in the State that does not include that place`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:911 | (2) A provision of the laws of the State is not to be taken to be a provision to which subsection (1) applies merely because it is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within Queensland waters, coastal waters or the adjacent area, however described, of the State.
@ref s 47B(2) (src:911-911)
GIVEN `the provision is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within Queensland waters, coastal waters or the adjacent area, however described, of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is taken to be a provision to which s 47B(1) applies merely because of that limit (s 47B(2))` IS
    IF `the provision is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within Queensland waters, coastal waters or the adjacent area, however described, of the State` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:913 | (1) A person who has a function or power conferred on the person under a law for the purposes of or in connection with a provision of the laws of the State has and may perform the function for the purposes of or in connection with that provision, as applying because of this part, as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State.
@ref s 47C(1) (src:913-913)
GIVEN `the person has a function or power conferred on the person under a law for the purposes of or in connection with a provision of the laws of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has and may perform the function as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State (s 47C(1))` IS
    IF `the person has a function or power conferred on the person under a law for the purposes of or in connection with a provision of the laws of the State` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:914 | (2) All courts of the State are invested with jurisdiction in all matters arising under the provisions of the laws of the State, as applying because of this part, as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State.
@ref s 47C(2) (src:914-914)
GIVEN `the matter arises under the provisions of the laws of the State, as applying because of this part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `all courts of the State are invested with jurisdiction in the matter (s 47C(2))` IS
    IF `the matter arises under the provisions of the laws of the State, as applying because of this part` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:916 | In addition to any other power under which the provisions of this part may be enacted, the provisions of this part are enacted under the legislative power of Parliament as extended by the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 5 and the Coastal Waters (State Title) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4.
@ref s 47D (src:916-916)
GIVEN `the power is the legislative power of Parliament as extended by the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 5 and the Coastal Waters (State Title) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisions of this part are enacted under the power (s 47D)` IS
    IF `the power is the legislative power of Parliament as extended by the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 5 and the Coastal Waters (State Title) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:918 | Nothing in this part limits any law, other than this part, that provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those laws, beyond the limits of the State.
@ref s 47E (src:918-918)
GIVEN `it is a law, other than this part, that provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those laws, beyond the limits of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this part limits the law (s 47E)` IS
    IF `it is a law, other than this part, that provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those laws, beyond the limits of the State` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

`the provisions the note to s 47E gives as examples of special application provisions` MEANS
    LIST "Fisheries Act 1994, section 11", "Offshore Minerals Act 1998, section 16", "Petroleum Act 1923, section 7A", "Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982, section 14"

-- The note says "for example": a provision on none of the lists is not answered.
-- src:919 | Note—
-- src:920 | Some Acts have special application provisions, for example, the following—
-- src:921 | • Fisheries Act 1994, section 11
-- src:922 | • Offshore Minerals Act 1998, section 16
-- src:923 | • Petroleum Act 1923, section 7A
-- src:924 | • Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982, section 14.
@ref s 47E, note (src:919-924)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is given in the note to s 47E as an example of a special application provision (s 47E, note)` IS
    IF elem provision `the provisions the note to s 47E gives as examples of special application provisions` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
